WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.893
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:16.163 --> 00:19.542
[theme music playing]

3
00:50.114 --> 00:55.119
LOVE IN DISGUISE

4
00:56.203 --> 00:58.539
[whimsical, suspenseful music playing]

5
00:58.622 --> 01:02.793
[cries out]

6
01:07.381 --> 01:09.258
[thudding]

7
01:11.969 --> 01:14.305
[chandelier crashing]

8
01:20.269 --> 01:21.979
[groans]

9
01:23.772 --> 01:25.065
[gasps] Oh, my God!

10
01:25.900 --> 01:27.610
[groaning]

11
01:28.068 --> 01:28.944
Are you all right?

12
01:29.528 --> 01:31.488
Yeah. [groans]

13
01:31.572 --> 01:34.116
Mr. Yoon! Are you hurt, sir?

14
01:34.783 --> 01:36.577
Don't worry about me right now!

15
01:37.202 --> 01:39.163
[groaning] That hurts…

16
01:40.122 --> 01:42.958
-[Yi-jun] Hold still. -Oh my goodness, Mr. Kang!

17
01:43.042 --> 01:44.835
Oh no, what on earth?

18
01:44.919 --> 01:46.086
What happened here?

19
01:46.170 --> 01:48.547
[gasps] Oh! Why did the chandelier…

20
01:49.214 --> 01:50.716
Oh, Mr. Yoon, are you all right, sir?

21
01:50.799 --> 01:53.385
-Get a first-aid kit. -Right, got it. I'll get one right away.

22
01:53.761 --> 01:55.971
-First-aid kit. I'll be right back! -Yes, hi there.

23
01:56.764 --> 01:58.515
I think we'll be coming by the hospital.

24
01:58.599 --> 02:00.142
I don't need to go to the hospital.

25
02:00.684 --> 02:02.561
-[grunts in pain] -Sure about that?

26
02:02.645 --> 02:03.729
[groans]

27
02:03.812 --> 02:05.189
We'll be there in ten minutes.

28
02:05.773 --> 02:08.025
Not for me, my secretary just got hurt--

29
02:09.234 --> 02:10.402
Actually, no, I'm fine.

30
02:10.486 --> 02:12.655
-Not necessary. -[call ends]

31
02:14.114 --> 02:16.325
-What the hell are you thinking? -There's nothing wrong with me.

32
02:16.408 --> 02:17.826
I don't even think I've broken anything.

33
02:19.244 --> 02:21.997
Here, here's the first-aid kit.

34
02:22.081 --> 02:22.957
This should be enough.

35
02:23.916 --> 02:25.125
[Yi-jun] What are you doing?

36
02:26.919 --> 02:28.337
Why are you acting like this?

37
02:29.672 --> 02:32.216
[Ms. Choi] Oh my… [whimpers]

38
02:41.809 --> 02:42.685
[groans]

39
02:48.148 --> 02:51.819
[groaning]

40
02:51.902 --> 02:54.822
[tense, dramatic music playing]

41
03:00.577 --> 03:02.079
[chandelier crashes]

42
03:03.080 --> 03:06.500
What the heck? How did it just suddenly fall?

43
03:06.583 --> 03:09.628
[Jae-hee] The lights seem dimmer than they were before I left yesterday.

44
03:09.712 --> 03:11.672
So I'm not the only one to notice it?

45
03:11.755 --> 03:14.925
Starting today, your role is to keep me safe.

46
03:15.009 --> 03:18.012
When I held the glass in my hand, I could tell the difference right then.

47
03:18.095 --> 03:21.181
So wouldn't that mean something was added to it?

48
03:21.265 --> 03:24.143
You're gonna learn what a dangerous world this is.

49
03:24.226 --> 03:25.686
I'm sure you know already.

50
03:34.236 --> 03:36.613
[Yi-jun] Why won't you just go to the hospital?

51
03:36.697 --> 03:37.781
[door handle rattling]

52
03:39.116 --> 03:40.701
[suspenseful music playing]

53
03:40.784 --> 03:41.785
Open up.

54
03:41.869 --> 03:42.870
[door handle rattling]

55
03:42.953 --> 03:45.080
Open the door. Open this door!

56
03:45.164 --> 03:46.373
Hey, I'll be right out.

57
03:46.457 --> 03:48.000
Open the door, I said!

58
03:48.083 --> 03:49.501
[Jae-hee] Seriously, sir, I'm barely hurt.

59
03:49.585 --> 03:51.754
-Ugh, Jesus… -[Yi-jun] Open it right now.

60
03:51.837 --> 03:54.298
I don't understand why you're so freaked out.

61
03:55.090 --> 03:57.593
[panting]

62
03:58.802 --> 04:01.764
[young Yi-jun] Mommy, open the door! Why aren't you opening it?

63
04:01.847 --> 04:04.224
[tense, eerie music playing]

64
04:06.185 --> 04:09.980
Mommy! Can you hear me?

65
04:10.064 --> 04:12.900
[panting]

66
04:21.366 --> 04:23.368
[young Yi-jun] Mommy?

67
04:23.452 --> 04:25.245
[panting]

68
04:28.749 --> 04:30.542
Hang on! Can't you just wait?!

69
04:30.626 --> 04:32.127
[tense, eerie music continues]

70
04:32.211 --> 04:33.212
Go get the keys!

71
04:33.962 --> 04:34.797
[Ms. Choi] Right away, sir!

72
04:34.880 --> 04:36.507
[grunts]

73
04:37.299 --> 04:39.426
Mr. Yoon, here, I've got the keys for you.

74
04:43.222 --> 04:44.973
Special Forces, are you okay?

75
04:45.474 --> 04:47.726
[panting]

76
04:52.397 --> 04:55.025
[tense, dramatic music playing]

77
04:59.613 --> 05:01.156
[breathing shakily]

78
05:06.578 --> 05:08.330
I'm fine. What about you?

79
05:09.540 --> 05:11.708
If you hadn't gotten out of the way back there,

80
05:11.792 --> 05:13.210
you seriously could've died.

81
05:14.253 --> 05:15.712
On my first day here,

82
05:15.796 --> 05:18.257
when you made it a point to tell me not to let my guard down,

83
05:18.340 --> 05:21.677
'cause this world was dangerous, that's what you meant?

84
05:21.760 --> 05:23.011
You're still being a prude, huh?

85
05:23.971 --> 05:25.848
Then fix your shirt. At least be consistent.

86
05:27.933 --> 05:30.310
It's basically just a scrape. I'll show you.

87
05:31.520 --> 05:33.397
No one gets hospitalized for this.

88
05:35.732 --> 05:36.984
Earlier on…

89
05:38.443 --> 05:40.821
I told you something strange is going on in this place.

90
05:42.364 --> 05:46.160
The thing you know about that I don't, what is it?

91
05:48.704 --> 05:49.830
[door closes]

92
06:00.883 --> 06:03.385
[soft, airy music playing]

93
06:10.726 --> 06:12.352
[groans]

94
06:12.895 --> 06:13.729
Don't be a baby.

95
06:15.981 --> 06:19.026
That story about the Special Forces, that's a lie, right?

96
06:19.109 --> 06:20.611
How are you still doubting me?

97
06:21.653 --> 06:23.488
I've saved your life, haven't I?

98
06:25.949 --> 06:27.576
Aren't you going to answer me?

99
06:28.994 --> 06:30.787
[soft, airy music continues]

100
06:32.039 --> 06:33.040
No.

101
06:34.416 --> 06:35.500
Nothing to say.

102
06:36.835 --> 06:38.295
Mm-hmm.

103
06:39.213 --> 06:40.172
So is it all over for me?

104
06:41.965 --> 06:43.634
This is where I get fired, right?

105
06:47.763 --> 06:49.723
-[yelps] -Stop moving.

106
06:59.900 --> 07:01.777
What the heck?! What's going on?!

107
07:01.860 --> 07:03.695
He saved you?! Did you get hurt?! [gasps]

108
07:03.779 --> 07:06.156
Holy crap, Mr. Kang, what happened to you?!

109
07:06.240 --> 07:08.742
You're bleeding?! What the heck, huh?!

110
07:08.825 --> 07:11.203
Hey, you're seriously just using Q-tips on that?

111
07:11.286 --> 07:12.579
That looks terrible, huh?

112
07:12.704 --> 07:14.289
You gotta get to a hospital!

113
07:14.373 --> 07:15.749
What the heck happened to the chandelier?

114
07:15.832 --> 07:17.292
[Si-hyun] Come on, what happened?

115
07:17.376 --> 07:19.294
A chandelier doesn't just fall on its own.

116
07:19.670 --> 07:22.422
Wow, I knew something fishy was going on.

117
07:22.506 --> 07:24.591
Is this why you hired Mr. Kang?

118
07:25.175 --> 07:26.218
[sighs]

119
07:26.301 --> 07:28.553
I knew they'd be coming at you from all sides,

120
07:28.637 --> 07:30.389
but this is crossing a line!

121
07:30.472 --> 07:31.932
You should tell the chairman this happened.

122
07:32.641 --> 07:34.101
I bet he saw it coming.

123
07:34.226 --> 07:35.560
Or by now he already knows.

124
07:35.644 --> 07:38.897
[scoffs] Scary stuff…

125
07:38.981 --> 07:40.607
He let this happen to you?

126
07:40.691 --> 07:43.235
We shouldn't be shocked. We know this is how he always works.

127
07:43.819 --> 07:44.820
We grew up with this.

128
07:45.654 --> 07:47.239
-[sighs] -To hell with fair play,

129
07:47.322 --> 07:48.407
I just want you to win.

130
07:49.199 --> 07:51.368
-Then you'll have my respect. -Who did it, then?

131
07:54.204 --> 07:55.163
Got any guesses?

132
07:55.247 --> 07:57.249
[tense music playing]

133
08:00.127 --> 08:01.044
You didn't get hurt?

134
08:01.545 --> 08:02.379
No, I'm fine, sir.

135
08:04.381 --> 08:05.632
Park Min-hwan's gone missing,

136
08:05.757 --> 08:09.803
and we're on his tail, but we're not the only ones.

137
08:09.886 --> 08:11.763
[gasps] Huh?

138
08:11.847 --> 08:13.473
[Captain Park] About that chandelier that fell…

139
08:13.557 --> 08:15.684
You're saying that you don't think it was an accident?

140
08:16.184 --> 08:17.894
Yoon Yi-jun seems to have expected it?

141
08:17.978 --> 08:19.521
[Jae-hee] I don't know what's going on.

142
08:19.604 --> 08:21.231
Weird things are happening.

143
08:21.565 --> 08:22.566
I can't explain it.

144
08:25.861 --> 08:28.238
I don't think there's anyone as good as him.

145
08:30.282 --> 08:31.199
So let's fix this?

146
08:31.283 --> 08:33.118
About what? What do you want?

147
08:33.201 --> 08:36.663
Are you trying to take back his dismissal and not look like a bad boss?

148
08:36.747 --> 08:38.457
A violation of the Labor Standards Act,

149
08:38.540 --> 08:40.959
how the firing was actually illegal, that should work.

150
08:41.043 --> 08:43.962
You need to give 30 days' notice under Article 26,

151
08:44.046 --> 08:45.797
and you did violate that rule.

152
08:45.881 --> 08:47.424
And I only told him today,

153
08:47.507 --> 08:48.675
so I guess it's invalidated.

154
08:48.759 --> 08:49.593
Guess he's gotta stay.

155
08:49.676 --> 08:51.470
Aww, look at your face.

156
08:51.553 --> 08:54.723
The thing is, none of that applies, since it wasn't that kind of contract.

157
08:54.806 --> 08:57.768
-You're the one who wrote it. -Yeah, 'cause you told me to.

158
09:00.103 --> 09:02.314
Whatever. Find a better way.

159
09:05.484 --> 09:06.818
[camera shutter clicks]

160
09:10.322 --> 09:12.366
[chain rattling]

161
09:19.456 --> 09:20.457
[Si-hyun] I'm taking off.

162
09:23.210 --> 09:24.378
Mr. Kang.

163
09:25.670 --> 09:28.882
You should go and get looked at, to make sure nothing's wrong.

164
09:29.341 --> 09:31.635
If you wait, it could be harder to get workers' compensation.

165
09:31.718 --> 09:32.969
It might not get covered.

166
09:33.053 --> 09:34.638
I won't ask for any, don't worry about that.

167
09:35.597 --> 09:38.517
Well, all right then. As you wish. Mm.

168
09:39.393 --> 09:40.268
Oh…

169
09:42.062 --> 09:42.979
Ah.

170
09:43.105 --> 09:46.775
Uh, well, if there's any problem, you just let me know.

171
09:46.858 --> 09:49.194
You've saved a third-generation chaebol's life,

172
09:49.277 --> 09:51.321
so I could get you a great compensation package.

173
09:51.405 --> 09:53.698
[sighs] Oh, okay, okay, fine.

174
09:53.782 --> 09:55.325
-I think it's time to go. -Uh-huh.

175
09:55.409 --> 09:56.410
Aren't you going?

176
09:56.660 --> 09:58.245
-Out. -[Si-hyun] Whoa.

177
09:58.328 --> 10:00.288
-The door's that way. -[inhales sharply]

178
10:00.372 --> 10:02.124
[quirky music playing]

179
10:02.207 --> 10:03.625
[sighs]

180
10:03.708 --> 10:05.877
And if you're fired while on medical leave,

181
10:05.961 --> 10:07.712
that dismissal would be invalid.

182
10:08.296 --> 10:10.799
It's a violation of Article 23 of the Labor Standards Act.

183
10:10.882 --> 10:13.260
Therefore, you can't be fired!

184
10:14.094 --> 10:15.053
How'd I do?

185
10:16.596 --> 10:18.473
-Go. -Eh?

186
10:18.557 --> 10:19.474
I said, go.

187
10:20.767 --> 10:22.185
You have an appointment.

188
10:23.311 --> 10:25.188
I don't think I do…

189
10:25.272 --> 10:26.106
No, just…

190
10:26.189 --> 10:28.316
-Oh, hey, wait a sec, Mr. Kim. -Huh?

191
10:28.400 --> 10:30.485
-Uh, Mr. Kim, is that true? -What?

192
10:30.569 --> 10:31.695
So I'm not fired?

193
10:32.279 --> 10:33.238
Uh-huh.

194
10:33.947 --> 10:34.948
Thank you, sir.

195
10:35.574 --> 10:36.741
Mr. Yoon!

196
10:37.200 --> 10:38.785
Actually, my arm really does hurt.

197
10:38.869 --> 10:40.912
I'll go get a doctor's note, okay?

198
10:41.621 --> 10:42.789
Follow me.

199
10:49.296 --> 10:51.798
[Jae-hee panting]

200
10:52.966 --> 10:54.676
That's the thing with emergencies…

201
10:55.385 --> 10:57.679
following exact protocol can get tricky,

202
10:58.388 --> 10:59.639
especially when every second counts.

203
11:00.223 --> 11:03.143
Without my reflexes, on-the-spot judgment,

204
11:03.226 --> 11:05.103
and incredibly steadfast composure,

205
11:05.187 --> 11:08.273
I think it's safe to say you wouldn't have survived that incident.

206
11:08.648 --> 11:11.109
[gentle, quirky music playing]

207
11:12.194 --> 11:15.614
What you're trying to say is, you just did something extraordinary.

208
11:16.448 --> 11:17.365
Yes, that's correct!

209
11:17.449 --> 11:18.950
And you want thanks?

210
11:19.034 --> 11:20.118
Yes, please, sir.

211
11:20.202 --> 11:21.369
That was simply your duty.

212
11:21.995 --> 11:23.413
Let's not exaggerate here.

213
11:23.997 --> 11:24.998
Right, sir.

214
11:26.625 --> 11:27.834
Tell me the truth.

215
11:29.836 --> 11:30.837
The forbidden room.

216
11:32.422 --> 11:33.548
You saw everything.

217
11:34.049 --> 11:36.635
-[tense music playing] -[gulps]

218
11:39.638 --> 11:40.889
[Jae-hee] There it is!

219
11:43.558 --> 11:45.685
MESSAGES NO ONGOING CONVERSATIONS

220
11:45.769 --> 11:47.187
Huh?

221
11:48.396 --> 11:49.856
[Jerry meows]

222
11:50.815 --> 11:52.025
What?

223
11:55.070 --> 11:57.614
God. I don't think this is her phone after all.

224
11:57.697 --> 11:59.741
It just happens to be the same model?

225
12:01.660 --> 12:03.245
[sighs]

226
12:07.499 --> 12:09.000
[rustling]

227
12:21.638 --> 12:24.641
[cheeky, whimsical music playing]

228
12:27.269 --> 12:28.687
Mmm… [clears throat]

229
12:29.563 --> 12:34.234
No, I… I just took a little peek for half a second.

230
12:35.527 --> 12:36.361
So you saw.

231
12:40.574 --> 12:42.826
That's exactly what I thought.

232
12:46.121 --> 12:47.539
And you had the gall…

233
12:49.124 --> 12:51.543
to leave, run away, and tell everyone?

234
12:51.626 --> 12:52.919
No, I… I wasn't running.

235
12:53.003 --> 12:54.379
What were you gonna tell them?

236
12:54.462 --> 12:56.590
What kind of rumors were you gonna spread?

237
12:56.673 --> 12:58.049
That your boss is insane?

238
12:58.883 --> 13:00.594
I wasn't… I mean you're the one who decided

239
13:00.677 --> 13:01.720
you wanted to get rid of me, sir.

240
13:01.803 --> 13:04.097
That reminds me. Why don't we discuss your dismissal?

241
13:04.180 --> 13:05.515
No, Mr. Yoon, please, stop, please!

242
13:06.600 --> 13:07.601
I'm sorry.

243
13:10.437 --> 13:11.563
It's withdrawn.

244
13:14.441 --> 13:16.401
Sir, is that really what you meant to say?

245
13:16.985 --> 13:17.819
Withdrawn?

246
13:19.821 --> 13:21.448
Maybe I'll withdraw the withdrawal.

247
13:25.994 --> 13:29.080
Sir, please just be straight with me. What's going on here?

248
13:29.164 --> 13:31.333
I thought it was clear I'd never tell you that.

249
13:32.584 --> 13:35.920
Now that I know I'll be working here, I won't feign ignorance.

250
13:36.338 --> 13:37.464
I wanna be prepared.

251
13:37.839 --> 13:38.715
Forget what you know.

252
13:39.841 --> 13:40.884
If I tell you everything,

253
13:42.010 --> 13:44.054
you'll just hate me more than you do already.

254
13:44.137 --> 13:46.056
[somber music playing]

255
13:46.139 --> 13:47.599
[sighs]

256
13:47.682 --> 13:49.392
Why do I have to be kept in the dark?

257
13:52.270 --> 13:53.396
You still don't trust me?

258
13:57.609 --> 13:58.860
I've warned you already.

259
13:59.361 --> 14:01.404
Know your place, don't cross boundaries.

260
14:01.821 --> 14:06.034
Why should I be impressed that you saved me from a falling chandelier?

261
14:06.117 --> 14:10.372
You're under the delusion that you've done something quite heroic.

262
14:10.455 --> 14:13.917
Why don't you just do what you're asked and collect the paycheck?

263
14:21.424 --> 14:22.300
[sighs]

264
14:26.680 --> 14:29.391
[suspenseful, dramatic music playing]

265
14:45.782 --> 14:47.784
[suspenseful, dramatic music continues]

266
14:51.079 --> 14:52.038
[aerosol spray hisses]

267
14:52.122 --> 14:53.206
Whoa, whoa.

268
14:53.289 --> 14:56.084
Oh, my gosh! Jesus, why?! I was…

269
14:56.167 --> 14:59.295
[screaming, groaning]

270
14:59.379 --> 15:01.339
[Si-hyun] Ugh, what is this stuff? What did you do?!

271
15:01.423 --> 15:04.050
[unsettling music playing]

272
15:04.134 --> 15:07.011
-[screaming continues] -Are you… are you all right?

273
15:07.095 --> 15:09.264
[Si-hyun screaming, groaning]

274
15:09.347 --> 15:13.393
[water gurgling]

275
15:15.353 --> 15:17.647
Oh. Wow.

276
15:18.189 --> 15:21.025
[breathing heavily]

277
15:21.109 --> 15:22.819
[groans]

278
15:23.945 --> 15:27.031
-[awkward music playing] -Hm? [sighs]

279
15:31.327 --> 15:32.579
[Hye-jung] I'm sorry.

280
15:32.662 --> 15:34.330
I honestly didn't know that was you.

281
15:36.040 --> 15:37.459
[chuckles]

282
15:38.918 --> 15:40.837
You apologizing, looking like that…

283
15:41.755 --> 15:43.089
it's cute, actually.

284
15:44.048 --> 15:45.008
Someone stalking you?

285
15:46.468 --> 15:48.136
Mm… Didn't you have work?

286
15:49.596 --> 15:50.972
I thought we were meeting up tomorrow.

287
15:51.848 --> 15:53.683
Oh, I left something here.

288
15:53.767 --> 15:56.227
[quirky music playing]

289
15:56.311 --> 15:58.772
I guess that's why you put on that necktie.

290
15:58.855 --> 16:00.774
Is it really that obvious?

291
16:01.941 --> 16:03.109
[sighs]

292
16:04.152 --> 16:05.111
You're too observant.

293
16:06.321 --> 16:08.865
The girls I usually date forget their lipstick,

294
16:08.948 --> 16:10.700
wallet, compact powder, et cetera in my car.

295
16:11.284 --> 16:14.621
But you never do, though I really wish you would.

296
16:14.704 --> 16:15.914
[chuckles]

297
16:15.997 --> 16:17.999
So, I… am I that obvious?

298
16:18.958 --> 16:21.669
[sighs] Kim Si-hyun's got a lot to learn.

299
16:22.170 --> 16:23.171
Sorry.

300
16:25.006 --> 16:26.257
[grunts]

301
16:38.978 --> 16:40.104
So this is really what you want?

302
16:40.188 --> 16:41.898
I'm not a backup plan, Si-hyun.

303
16:42.607 --> 16:45.109
I don't want to be your plan B because your other plan fell through.

304
16:48.279 --> 16:49.197
[sighs]

305
16:50.031 --> 16:52.367
Okay, but I know what this is.

306
16:53.117 --> 16:55.203
You're only interested in me for my work.

307
16:56.746 --> 16:59.123
"What's going on in the chairman's office?"

308
16:59.207 --> 17:02.001
"Are they gonna hand control over to Mr. Yoon?"

309
17:02.877 --> 17:05.755
That's why you asked me out, right?

310
17:07.715 --> 17:08.758
See you later.

311
17:15.473 --> 17:16.391
Oh.

312
17:17.267 --> 17:18.518
The other thing didn't fall through.

313
17:19.602 --> 17:20.728
I wanted to see you.

314
17:21.896 --> 17:24.399
Anyway, whether we go out for dinner or not,

315
17:24.482 --> 17:26.150
I'll leave that up to you.

316
17:26.943 --> 17:29.070
[cheeky pensive piano music playing]

317
17:29.153 --> 17:30.655
-[door opens] -[door lock chimes]

318
17:31.614 --> 17:33.116
-[door closes] -[door lock chimes]

319
17:35.076 --> 17:36.369
[investigator] Oh, it's been cut.

320
17:37.287 --> 17:39.664
Cutting something with pliers, wire cutters, or bolt cutters

321
17:39.747 --> 17:41.124
leaves this kind of surface mark.

322
17:41.207 --> 17:42.750
It was definitely cut.

323
17:44.168 --> 17:45.670
So someone severed it?

324
17:46.462 --> 17:47.839
What kind of psycho would do that?

325
17:48.923 --> 17:50.216
[investigator] Who were they after?

326
17:50.300 --> 17:53.261
[pensive music playing]

327
18:05.398 --> 18:06.274
[Yi-jun] Really?

328
18:06.816 --> 18:09.152
You can send this thing flying with just a kick?

329
18:10.778 --> 18:13.114
-[groans in pain] -[whimsical music playing]

330
18:18.578 --> 18:19.954
[groaning]

331
18:20.038 --> 18:22.665
[rain pouring]

332
18:22.749 --> 18:24.792
[car horn beeping]

333
18:31.257 --> 18:32.300
[sighs]

334
18:34.510 --> 18:37.513
[gentle music playing]

335
18:40.683 --> 18:43.311
Mr. Kim, what are you doing here?

336
18:44.062 --> 18:45.772
Let's go. They're waiting.

337
18:45.855 --> 18:47.023
You came to get me?

338
18:47.941 --> 18:49.776
-I pulled the short straw. -Mm.

339
18:50.026 --> 18:52.695
Hey, you only brought one? There are several around the precinct.

340
18:53.446 --> 18:54.447
Oh, were there?

341
18:58.409 --> 19:00.036
[Seok-jin] I heard it was a close call.

342
19:00.119 --> 19:01.704
You really gotta be careful.

343
19:01.996 --> 19:04.624
When I saw what was happening, I acted reflexively.

344
19:06.376 --> 19:07.251
Why?

345
19:08.044 --> 19:10.004
You know, he's central to the investigation,

346
19:10.088 --> 19:11.089
it was just a quirk of--

347
19:11.172 --> 19:12.298
[Seok-jin] It doesn't matter, you could've gotten hurt.

348
19:12.382 --> 19:15.051
Rapport is important, but he's not worth it.

349
19:16.177 --> 19:17.512
Yep. I'll remember that.

350
19:24.352 --> 19:25.520
[Jae-hee] Oh, so this is it?

351
19:27.146 --> 19:29.399
[Ms. Han] Do you really think I'm going to make this easy for you?

352
19:29.482 --> 19:31.985
[Yi-jun] I thought I told you to stop being so clingy.

353
19:32.068 --> 19:34.821
Next time, you won't get off with just a warning.

354
19:36.531 --> 19:37.657
[Ms. Han] What are you gonna do?

355
19:37.740 --> 19:40.118
[ominous music playing]

356
19:48.167 --> 19:49.419
Do you smoke?

357
19:51.421 --> 19:52.338
You don't?

358
19:53.881 --> 19:56.342
Actually, this smoking habit of mine

359
19:57.719 --> 19:59.679
is the reason I saw what I did.

360
20:00.555 --> 20:03.099
[tense synth music playing]

361
20:11.899 --> 20:15.319
What if Yoon Yi-jun didn't kill Ms. Han after all?

362
20:17.030 --> 20:18.656
That'd throw a wrench in things.

363
20:23.578 --> 20:24.871
I recognize her,

364
20:24.954 --> 20:26.831
-Tae-sik's second-eldest, right? -That's right.

365
20:26.914 --> 20:29.417
-Yoon Na-jung. -[Wan-gu] Hang on a second.

366
20:29.500 --> 20:33.421
The person who tipped us off, could that've actually been her?

367
20:33.504 --> 20:34.672
Could've been her.

368
20:34.756 --> 20:36.716
Okay, but even the most heartless people

369
20:36.799 --> 20:40.344
feel a protective instinct toward their younger siblings, don't they?

370
20:41.012 --> 20:42.930
About the Han Eun-young case,

371
20:43.556 --> 20:45.892
why would it happen right now, at the very moment

372
20:45.975 --> 20:48.895
when the media's focused on Yi-jun as the company's heir?

373
20:48.978 --> 20:51.981
So then, should we start viewing this as a battle for succession?

374
20:53.149 --> 20:57.028
Yes, it's true that when Yi-jun was made the prime murder suspect,

375
20:57.111 --> 20:58.362
Yoon Na-jung stood to gain.

376
20:58.863 --> 21:00.406
TAEKANG RETAIL STOCK PURCHASE AGREEMENT

377
21:00.490 --> 21:03.117
[tense, dramatic music playing]

378
21:04.077 --> 21:05.745
SELLER NAME: YOON TAE-SIK

379
21:05.828 --> 21:09.916
One thing's clear, he sure loves his son a whole lot.

380
21:17.381 --> 21:21.094
He'll make the line of succession clear at our next meeting.

381
21:21.886 --> 21:23.679
And I imagine you're looking forward to that,

382
21:25.098 --> 21:25.973
if I'm not mistaken?

383
21:26.057 --> 21:27.308
[thuds]

384
21:31.979 --> 21:33.356
Don't even try me, Si-hyun.

385
21:34.649 --> 21:38.653
When I get angry, there's no predicting how I'll act.

386
21:39.904 --> 21:43.199
[Seok-jin] I don't know. Even if that was Yoon Na-jung's goal,

387
21:43.282 --> 21:45.326
that might just mean we have another witness.

388
21:45.409 --> 21:47.620
It wouldn't clear Yoon Yi-jun of all charges.

389
21:49.539 --> 21:51.415
-Ugh, my head hurts. -Yeah, that's the issue.

390
21:51.541 --> 21:53.251
[phone buzzing]

391
21:54.877 --> 21:56.170
Hi. Anything?

392
21:58.673 --> 21:59.841
Got it, thanks.

393
22:01.092 --> 22:03.010
-[call ends] -That's NFS with the results.

394
22:03.094 --> 22:04.512
Detective Kang was right.

395
22:04.887 --> 22:07.306
They confirmed they found high levels of herbicide in the milk.

396
22:07.390 --> 22:08.599
Hm?

397
22:08.683 --> 22:10.726
-Shi… -[Wan-gu] God. Why does everything

398
22:10.810 --> 22:12.687
have to be so shady?

399
22:13.354 --> 22:15.940
That phone you just found, it wasn't Han Eun-young's, right?

400
22:16.023 --> 22:17.525
Right. I looked into that,

401
22:17.608 --> 22:20.695
apparently it's a model given to all Taekang personnel three years back.

402
22:20.778 --> 22:21.821
It wasn't just Yi-jun.

403
22:21.904 --> 22:23.531
Mr. Jung had been using the exact same one too.

404
22:23.614 --> 22:24.490
[hums thoughtfully]

405
22:24.574 --> 22:26.826
Why was Yoon Yi-jun acting like that?

406
22:26.909 --> 22:29.453
I don't get why that room is so forbidden.

407
22:29.537 --> 22:31.497
He was acting like something's in there.

408
22:31.914 --> 22:33.708
What's that room used for then?

409
22:34.125 --> 22:35.793
[curious musical sting]

410
22:36.419 --> 22:39.005
Uh, it's sort of… um…

411
22:39.589 --> 22:40.715
[curious musical sting]

412
22:40.798 --> 22:43.050
…sort of a room for his hobbies. Yeah.

413
22:43.134 --> 22:46.387
You know, the kind of secret hobby you'd wanna keep private.

414
22:49.223 --> 22:50.224
A chaebol?

415
22:50.308 --> 22:51.642
Secret hobby?

416
22:53.019 --> 22:55.146
Tell me, why would you want that?

417
22:55.229 --> 22:57.064
[fireworks popping]

418
22:57.148 --> 23:00.151
[swinging jazz music playing]

419
23:07.950 --> 23:10.244
[sultry pop music playing]

420
23:11.662 --> 23:12.914
[whip cracks]

421
23:13.915 --> 23:15.333
Mmm…

422
23:16.250 --> 23:17.501
[sultry growl]

423
23:20.254 --> 23:22.089
[groans, munches]

424
23:23.216 --> 23:26.177
[upbeat rock music playing]

425
23:30.097 --> 23:31.474
[gunshots]

426
23:33.100 --> 23:34.268
[gunshots]

427
23:36.062 --> 23:37.980
[laughing maniacally]

428
23:38.064 --> 23:41.275
[laughing maniacally]

429
23:41.359 --> 23:42.777
[music ends]

430
23:45.613 --> 23:47.073
[Jae-hee] Ugh, stop it, you guys!

431
23:47.990 --> 23:50.743
Seriously! What are you even suggesting?

432
23:50.826 --> 23:52.870
Gross! It was nothing special.

433
23:53.704 --> 23:56.165
And he caught me while I was in there looking for the phone.

434
23:56.249 --> 23:57.250
You certain?

435
23:58.042 --> 24:00.086
It's not his secret sexy fun room, are you sure?

436
24:00.169 --> 24:02.713
Wan-gu, God! You're really crossing my boundaries.

437
24:02.797 --> 24:04.298
Please keep your theories to yourself.

438
24:04.382 --> 24:05.716
Oh, come on.

439
24:05.800 --> 24:07.718
It's whatever. It's not a big deal.

440
24:07.802 --> 24:10.471
"Crossing your boundaries," who gives a crap?!

441
24:10.554 --> 24:12.682
[Wan-gu] I'm just using my imagination here, who cares?

442
24:12.765 --> 24:14.600
Know your place, don't cross boundaries.

443
24:14.684 --> 24:16.018
[Yi-jun] Forget what you know.

444
24:16.519 --> 24:17.603
If I tell you everything,

445
24:17.687 --> 24:19.814
you'll just hate me more than you do already.

446
24:24.026 --> 24:26.445
I thought I told you to stop being so clingy.

447
24:26.529 --> 24:28.531
[in video] Next time, you won't get off with just a warning.

448
24:28.614 --> 24:29.615
Wait a minute.

449
24:29.699 --> 24:32.702
[Yi-jun in video] I don't know yet. If you were to keep this up…

450
24:32.785 --> 24:35.079
[sighs] …there's just no telling what I would do to you.

451
24:35.913 --> 24:39.834
Have you thought… Yoon Yi-jun actually wasn't threatening her in this video?

452
24:39.917 --> 24:42.295
-How's that? -Huh?

453
24:42.378 --> 24:44.463
He's worried he'll put her in harm's way.

454
24:44.547 --> 24:45.715
He wants to protect her.

455
24:46.382 --> 24:47.842
He said a similar thing to me.

456
24:47.925 --> 24:49.927
Are you saying Yoon Yi-jun should be ruled out?

457
24:50.011 --> 24:52.305
I'm not. I'm just talking hypothetically.

458
24:53.139 --> 24:54.849
If we do rule out Yoon Yi-jun,

459
24:54.932 --> 24:58.019
that explains the chandelier, the poisoning attempt,

460
24:58.102 --> 25:00.896
going after Park Min-hwan, and even Yoon Na-jung?

461
25:00.980 --> 25:03.316
That's a good theory. There's something there.

462
25:03.399 --> 25:04.692
Okay.

463
25:06.360 --> 25:08.696
When you hit a dead end, you go back to square one.

464
25:08.779 --> 25:09.905
Let's start over,

465
25:10.531 --> 25:13.868
with the understanding that Yi-jun may not be the murderer.

466
25:13.951 --> 25:15.202
Let's revisit everything.

467
25:15.286 --> 25:16.579
-Right! -Got it!

468
25:20.499 --> 25:22.543
[phone buzzing]

469
25:25.796 --> 25:27.548
-Yes, sir! -[Seok-jin] Are there any other lists?

470
25:27.631 --> 25:29.383
That's the only record of recent visitors.

471
25:29.467 --> 25:32.595
[Seok-jin] We looked it over, everyone's IDs checked out.

472
25:32.678 --> 25:34.388
You're absolutely sure all of them do?

473
25:35.598 --> 25:39.185
Choi Myeong-suk and Kim Si-hyun were the only ones who could've entered freely.

474
25:40.227 --> 25:41.604
Okay, understood.

475
25:41.687 --> 25:45.274
[pensive music playing]

476
25:46.275 --> 25:47.902
[Jae-hee] Ms. Choi, let me help you with that.

477
25:48.652 --> 25:50.946
Oh, thank you. Really, there's no need.

478
25:51.822 --> 25:52.823
Gosh.

479
25:53.407 --> 25:56.118
How do you always have such quick reflexes?

480
25:56.202 --> 25:57.912
Goodness. If it weren't for you,

481
25:58.037 --> 26:00.331
something awful could've happened to Mr. Yoon.

482
26:01.123 --> 26:05.086
Actually, you know the milk Mr. Yoon drinks when he has trouble sleeping?

483
26:06.170 --> 26:07.922
Why does Mr. Kim always bring it?

484
26:08.005 --> 26:10.299
Aren't you typically the one in charge of the food here?

485
26:10.383 --> 26:14.762
Yeah, I forget where it's from. Italy or Denmark.

486
26:14.845 --> 26:16.764
But it's imported and organic.

487
26:16.847 --> 26:19.392
It's from an imported food store near Mr. Kim's house.

488
26:21.519 --> 26:23.437
-Is that so? -And since he comes by

489
26:23.521 --> 26:25.481
to visit Mr. Yoon fairly regularly,

490
26:25.564 --> 26:27.441
he just picks it up on his way over.

491
26:28.567 --> 26:30.653
It's one less thing for me to take care of.

492
26:30.736 --> 26:33.197
As far as I'm concerned, he can do it.

493
26:33.280 --> 26:35.616
[chuckles]

494
26:35.699 --> 26:38.035
[mysterious music playing]

495
26:38.119 --> 26:40.746
-Let's chat when you're done. [chuckles] -Okay.

496
26:42.790 --> 26:45.876
[sighs] Kim Si-hyun, I wonder…

497
26:47.378 --> 26:48.504
[sighs]

498
26:51.006 --> 26:52.675
Your insomnia's back, isn't it?

499
26:53.426 --> 26:54.260
How long's it been?

500
26:55.803 --> 26:57.555
You seem to have slept like a king.

501
26:58.514 --> 26:59.765
So what do you care?

502
27:02.560 --> 27:03.853
I worry about you.

503
27:05.396 --> 27:06.605
Are you being serious?

504
27:07.440 --> 27:09.608
I thought you were gonna call, and then you didn't.

505
27:09.692 --> 27:11.110
What?

506
27:11.193 --> 27:13.446
Ugh, I won't let this go on. Get up, sir.

507
27:14.155 --> 27:15.322
All right, come on.

508
27:15.406 --> 27:18.284
[chill, jazz music playing]

509
27:18.367 --> 27:21.745
[Jae-hee] A vitamin D deficiency can negatively impact sleep quality.

510
27:21.829 --> 27:24.248
Everyone needs a dose of sunlight three times per week,

511
27:24.331 --> 27:25.833
and that's been scientifically proven.

512
27:25.916 --> 27:28.669
Especially if they're the type to regularly hole up

513
27:28.752 --> 27:29.920
in their house, like you do.

514
27:30.004 --> 27:31.839
I don't "hole up in my house."

515
27:31.922 --> 27:33.549
I'm not as bad as you're saying.

516
27:33.632 --> 27:35.676
I don't know, I'd say you're pretty bad.

517
27:35.759 --> 27:38.429
You're a reclusive loner with antisocial tendencies.

518
27:40.347 --> 27:43.350
Normally, Taekang employees keep their thoughts to themselves.

519
27:43.434 --> 27:45.269
Why don't you try it for once?

520
27:45.352 --> 27:47.813
Gimme a break. Come on! Move your body a little.

521
27:47.897 --> 27:49.273
Here! Walk harder.

522
27:49.356 --> 27:53.194
When you're stuck on your thoughts, you should try moving your body around.

523
27:53.277 --> 27:56.197
-One, two, one, two. -How dare you treat me like your pet?

524
27:56.697 --> 27:57.615
Oh.

525
27:57.698 --> 27:59.783
I'll be walking however I want, so leave me alone.

526
27:59.992 --> 28:02.995
[sighs] Okay. Let's try going for a little run,

527
28:03.078 --> 28:04.622
you can do it however you want.

528
28:04.705 --> 28:06.957
Let's just make it over there. Okay.

529
28:07.041 --> 28:08.959
-One, three! -I will not.

530
28:09.460 --> 28:10.920
And you skipped over number two.

531
28:11.629 --> 28:13.756
-Oh! -Whoa!

532
28:13.839 --> 28:16.592
[soft, shimmering music playing]

533
28:22.097 --> 28:23.432
[sighs]

534
28:23.516 --> 28:24.558
What was that?

535
28:25.351 --> 28:26.477
Was I actually in danger?

536
28:26.560 --> 28:29.480
Well, sure, I'd say it was a pretty close call.

537
28:30.064 --> 28:31.982
Oh, I was scared. Let's go.

538
28:41.825 --> 28:43.077
I wanna talk.

539
28:43.160 --> 28:45.246
We barely walked at all, how are you already tired?

540
28:45.329 --> 28:46.163
-[sighs] -[man] Here, catch!

541
28:47.039 --> 28:47.957
Whoa!

542
28:51.001 --> 28:53.212
[pants] Thank you, mister.

543
28:55.631 --> 28:57.049
[playful music playing]

544
28:57.132 --> 28:58.509
Just calm down and sit.

545
29:02.513 --> 29:04.348
Why are you so overprotective?

546
29:06.559 --> 29:09.311
Looking back on your actions these last few days,

547
29:09.395 --> 29:11.730
you've been acting weirdly…

548
29:13.899 --> 29:14.775
considerate.

549
29:15.985 --> 29:17.152
Nicer than usual.

550
29:17.903 --> 29:18.821
[Jae-hee] Really?

551
29:19.446 --> 29:22.700
Up until recently, you were looking at me with contempt.

552
29:25.202 --> 29:27.246
I'm not sure if it's the sleeplessness

553
29:27.329 --> 29:29.415
or the lack of sunlight that's messing with you,

554
29:29.498 --> 29:31.250
but you sound insane.

555
29:31.834 --> 29:34.295
You realize when that chandelier was falling on you,

556
29:34.378 --> 29:35.754
you barely even reacted?

557
29:36.380 --> 29:39.675
If I hadn't been next to you right then, you'd be dead right now.

558
29:40.426 --> 29:41.844
You'd be up in heaven.

559
29:42.177 --> 29:44.305
You told me to know my place and do my job,

560
29:44.388 --> 29:45.472
so what do you expect?

561
29:45.889 --> 29:47.641
Isn't my job to provide protection?

562
29:47.725 --> 29:49.268
I think you got the wrong idea.

563
29:49.727 --> 29:52.104
You think my taking you back means you can act out?

564
29:55.316 --> 29:57.568
Well, I suppose you're right.

565
30:00.446 --> 30:02.281
How'd you get so close with Kim Si-hyun?

566
30:04.283 --> 30:05.492
Excuse me?

567
30:08.078 --> 30:11.624
I mean, wouldn't you say that he's the closest friend you have?

568
30:13.042 --> 30:14.793
I'm just wondering why…

569
30:15.919 --> 30:19.089
Kim Si-hyun is a person of interest all of a sudden.

570
30:21.216 --> 30:24.053
[tense music playing]

571
30:24.136 --> 30:25.137
TAEKANG RETAIL STOCK PURCHASE AGREEMENT

572
30:25.220 --> 30:28.557
Preparations for Yoon Yi-jun's succession are almost complete, Mr. Chairman.

573
30:34.647 --> 30:36.523
-[Tae-sik] Ms. Lee. -[Hye-jung] Yes, sir.

574
30:38.984 --> 30:41.987
-Make sure Yi-jun attends the meeting. -[Hye-jung] I will, sir.

575
30:42.071 --> 30:44.365
I'll send a reminder through the secretarial office.

576
31:02.966 --> 31:03.842
Have you decided?

577
31:04.510 --> 31:05.552
Are we going out for dinner?

578
31:05.636 --> 31:07.471
I like things out in the open.

579
31:08.055 --> 31:10.974
That applies to my diet, my itinerary, who I date.

580
31:11.975 --> 31:14.061
-Just so you know. -How generous.

581
31:14.144 --> 31:16.814
You'd even stoop down to date a man from your past?

582
31:16.897 --> 31:19.483
Whether you stay an ex or we date again,

583
31:19.566 --> 31:20.943
that's entirely up to you.

584
31:23.821 --> 31:25.030
Entirely up to me?

585
31:28.450 --> 31:30.994
[tense music playing]

586
31:34.373 --> 31:37.000
So you're gonna hand this over to Yoon Yi-jun today?

587
31:39.420 --> 31:42.005
He did, he didn't.

588
31:43.424 --> 31:46.135
He killed her, he didn't kill her.

589
31:47.261 --> 31:49.680
I know you could settle this with a single word,

590
31:49.763 --> 31:51.640
I just figured I could help you out.

591
31:56.103 --> 31:58.689
In accounting, there's a manager named Park Min-hwan.

592
31:59.523 --> 32:02.568
[thunder rumbling]

593
32:02.651 --> 32:05.112
[suspenseful music playing]

594
32:09.450 --> 32:12.745
[Na-jung] He's the only one who knows who did what that day.

595
32:13.370 --> 32:16.039
But the thing is, he's gone AWOL.

596
32:17.332 --> 32:20.127
And worse, apparently he's not empty-handed.

597
32:21.879 --> 32:23.297
Aren't you curious, Dad?

598
32:24.214 --> 32:26.842
Don't you wanna know what he's been up to behind your back?

599
32:29.178 --> 32:32.222
-[sighs] Get to the point. -He's not your only child, you know.

600
32:32.806 --> 32:34.433
So reconsider.

601
32:42.941 --> 32:45.027
They say it's imperative you attend the meeting.

602
32:45.110 --> 32:46.236
I'm not going.

603
32:46.361 --> 32:47.571
I'll get in trouble if you don't.

604
32:47.654 --> 32:48.906
Well, then that's your problem.

605
32:48.989 --> 32:49.990
Get lost.

606
32:50.073 --> 32:53.118
Please, Mr. Yoon, the chairman himself is demanding that you show up.

607
32:53.827 --> 32:56.413
Yeah, well, he never asked directly. Get lost!

608
32:56.497 --> 32:58.373
Ugh, Mr. Yoon, just this once!

609
32:58.457 --> 32:59.833
Just this once…

610
33:01.043 --> 33:03.712
Was I not clear? Get lost.

611
33:03.796 --> 33:05.672
Oh, what the hell! Just go to it!

612
33:05.756 --> 33:07.257
Get out!

613
33:07.341 --> 33:08.383
You're being a nuisance.

614
33:08.467 --> 33:10.010
I saved your life, for God's sake.

615
33:10.093 --> 33:11.094
Just one favor.

616
33:11.178 --> 33:12.846
[Jae-hee] Just go!

617
33:14.097 --> 33:15.974
[screams in frustration] Why did I even save him?

618
33:16.058 --> 33:19.269
Ugh, seriously, why?! Shouldn't have bothered. [sighs]

619
33:22.689 --> 33:23.857
[sighs]

620
33:27.861 --> 33:29.363
SECRETARY LEE HYE-JUNG

621
33:30.989 --> 33:33.659
Yes, hello? Hi, Ms. Lee, it's Jae-hee.

622
33:34.284 --> 33:36.829
[Jae-hee] Mr. Jung said I should get in touch with you.

623
33:37.538 --> 33:38.705
Uh-huh.

624
33:39.289 --> 33:42.251
I'm so sorry, it seems Mr. Yoon can't attend today's meeting.

625
33:42.334 --> 33:43.794
Oh, dear.

626
33:44.586 --> 33:48.382
If the star of the show doesn't come, that'll really put a damper on things.

627
33:48.465 --> 33:49.758
[tense musical sting]

628
33:51.510 --> 33:55.055
When you gave me your business card, you said I could ask you stuff.

629
33:55.138 --> 33:57.057
Yes. What is it?

630
33:57.140 --> 33:59.726
Why is it so important that Mr. Yoon come to this one?

631
33:59.810 --> 34:01.728
Well, I think it's what you are assuming.

632
34:01.812 --> 34:04.565
The chairman is planning to name his successor.

633
34:05.816 --> 34:07.025
Well, in that case,

634
34:07.109 --> 34:10.153
that means that, uh, the entire family will attend, right?

635
34:10.237 --> 34:11.530
Everyone, without exception.

636
34:11.613 --> 34:13.448
[upbeat music playing]

637
34:13.532 --> 34:16.076
Everyone, without exception?

638
34:17.119 --> 34:18.245
Understood.

639
34:21.415 --> 34:22.624
[knocking on door]

640
34:22.708 --> 34:23.584
Don't come in.

641
34:25.252 --> 34:26.295
-[music ends] -[door closes]

642
34:27.462 --> 34:29.089
Why do you even bother knocking?

643
34:29.673 --> 34:31.550
I would like to make a bet with you.

644
34:31.633 --> 34:34.428
If you lose it, you'll go to the meeting.

645
34:34.511 --> 34:38.307
That won't be happening. I will not be making any bets.

646
34:38.390 --> 34:40.100
There is just no way.

647
34:40.183 --> 34:42.227
If I win, I won't file a report.

648
34:42.895 --> 34:44.104
No one will find out.

649
34:44.187 --> 34:45.022
About?

650
34:45.522 --> 34:46.857
The chandelier falling on you.

651
34:47.691 --> 34:49.985
As your secretary, I have to file a report.

652
34:51.528 --> 34:54.865
-First of all, I'm your boss. -Mm-mm.

653
34:54.948 --> 34:57.075
I'm a Taekang secretarial team member.

654
34:57.159 --> 34:59.870
I suppose the chairman will eventually find out

655
34:59.953 --> 35:03.040
through his secretary, if I do file a report.

656
35:03.123 --> 35:04.207
Are you threatening me?

657
35:04.291 --> 35:05.500
Cooperate with me.

658
35:05.584 --> 35:08.378
Suspicious things have been happening around you recently,

659
35:08.462 --> 35:11.465
and yet, you still haven't told the police about any of it.

660
35:11.548 --> 35:14.343
I think you'd be in a tough spot if your dad found out,

661
35:14.426 --> 35:16.219
or, worst case, the public.

662
35:16.303 --> 35:18.513
I told you not to address me like this.

663
35:18.597 --> 35:21.600
If you don't go to the meeting, I'm the one who will get blamed for it,

664
35:21.683 --> 35:24.227
and after that, I'll be forced to tell them all the truth.

665
35:24.311 --> 35:27.105
So carefully consider whether you want my cooperation.

666
35:27.189 --> 35:28.398
Think it over.

667
35:29.358 --> 35:30.567
[scoffs]

668
35:32.527 --> 35:34.571
What is it? The bet?

669
35:34.655 --> 35:38.075
[mischievous music playing]

670
35:38.575 --> 35:39.660
[bell dings]

671
35:39.743 --> 35:42.245
You're sneaky. You had to make this about strength?

672
35:42.329 --> 35:44.164
Don't you see I'm evening the playing field?

673
35:44.247 --> 35:46.708
Want something else? Boxing, jiu-jitsu, anything you want.

674
35:46.792 --> 35:48.543
You do realize I regularly take

675
35:48.627 --> 35:51.129
deer antler velvet and ginseng to build strength.

676
35:51.213 --> 35:53.924
Yeah, sure. Just be ready to get going when I win.

677
35:54.007 --> 35:56.593
And when I win, let's forget all about the chandelier.

678
35:56.677 --> 35:59.262
[gasps] How does a man have hands like this?

679
35:59.346 --> 36:00.889
You've clearly never had a day of work.

680
36:00.973 --> 36:01.974
How're yours so small?

681
36:02.057 --> 36:03.642
This could belong to a young lady.

682
36:03.725 --> 36:05.227
No, they're not.

683
36:05.310 --> 36:07.562
-They're big. -Oh.

684
36:08.563 --> 36:10.190
[both breathing heavily]

685
36:10.691 --> 36:12.985
[Jae-hee] I'll be at a disadvantage if this drags on.

686
36:13.485 --> 36:15.195
Force is proportional to velocity.

687
36:15.278 --> 36:18.448
Okay, I'll use my speed to end this as soon as I can.

688
36:18.532 --> 36:19.950
[whistle blows]

689
36:20.909 --> 36:22.661
-[chuckles] -[gasps]

690
36:26.248 --> 36:27.958
[ominous music playing]

691
36:30.002 --> 36:32.546
-[energetic, confident music playing] -[Yi-jun grunting]

692
36:34.131 --> 36:36.216
[grunting]

693
36:51.440 --> 36:54.901
-[record scratches] -Mmm…

694
36:56.153 --> 36:57.821
[blows air]

695
36:58.530 --> 36:59.781
[thuds]

696
36:59.865 --> 37:01.908
-[gasps] -[whistle blows]

697
37:01.992 --> 37:04.619
[both scream triumphantly]

698
37:06.621 --> 37:08.081
Yay!

699
37:08.165 --> 37:09.249
[gasps]

700
37:10.834 --> 37:14.588
-You cheated! I'm on to you! -Well, I learned from the best, didn't I?

701
37:16.840 --> 37:18.008
I guess I win.

702
37:19.134 --> 37:20.302
[sighs]

703
37:21.386 --> 37:23.055
Again! Best out of three.

704
37:23.138 --> 37:24.097
Mm-hm-mm.

705
37:24.181 --> 37:26.641
You're the one who wanted one round.

706
37:26.725 --> 37:28.477
I must get going now, sir.

707
37:29.144 --> 37:30.687
[Yi-jun] Where are you going?

708
37:31.188 --> 37:33.315
Get dressed and ready to go.

709
37:33.899 --> 37:34.900
[cheers]

710
37:35.484 --> 37:37.861
[screams] I lost!

711
37:39.738 --> 37:41.406
[Jae-hee] I'll go see Yoon Na-jung

712
37:41.490 --> 37:44.284
to figure out whether she's a suspect or just another witness.

713
37:56.963 --> 37:59.633
I get in the car however I want. What?

714
38:06.765 --> 38:09.726
[sighs] Four-year-old children have more maturity.

715
38:10.185 --> 38:11.561
Why does he talk like that?

716
38:12.062 --> 38:13.105
[snorts]

717
38:22.322 --> 38:23.281
[knocking on door]

718
38:28.495 --> 38:30.872
Everyone appears set to arrive on time, sir.

719
38:35.585 --> 38:36.920
If you want him as your successor,

720
38:37.420 --> 38:40.298
why not wait until things are more settled down?

721
38:47.514 --> 38:50.684
I'll get them settled. Things won't be solved on their own.

722
38:51.434 --> 38:52.811
I just worry about the kid.

723
38:54.771 --> 38:55.939
He's my own blood after all.

724
38:57.482 --> 38:59.234
Anything can be dangerous when rushed.

725
38:59.317 --> 39:02.988
Shouldn't he stabilize a little, before taking on more work?

726
39:03.071 --> 39:05.031
If this is more than he can handle,

727
39:05.991 --> 39:07.909
I'd rather find out quickly.

728
39:07.993 --> 39:11.496
Right. You should hand over control and retire.

729
39:12.539 --> 39:15.625
And I also look forward to taking a step back and playing some golf.

730
39:15.709 --> 39:18.420
[both chuckle]

731
39:28.722 --> 39:29.723
[teen] Mom.

732
39:30.182 --> 39:31.391
Oh, there you are!

733
39:31.474 --> 39:33.935
Ugh, do I really have to go to this?

734
39:34.311 --> 39:36.938
Shouldn't I be studying instead of going to a coronation?

735
39:37.022 --> 39:39.858
Ka-on, you've always been close to your uncle.

736
39:39.941 --> 39:42.194
And that's a good reason why.

737
39:42.986 --> 39:45.614
Who knows, he might give me a subsidiary someday.

738
39:45.697 --> 39:47.240
[chuckles] So mine's not enough, now?

739
39:47.324 --> 39:49.159
Where'd you learn to be so greedy, honey?

740
39:49.242 --> 39:51.953
I did inherit one quarter of Yoon Tae-sik's blood, didn't I?

741
39:52.037 --> 39:54.372
-Why aren't you greedier? -[laughs]

742
39:55.290 --> 39:58.418
[tense, dramatic music playing]

743
40:36.581 --> 40:38.124
[music fades]

744
40:40.001 --> 40:41.962
[secretary 1] The day's finally here, huh?

745
40:42.045 --> 40:44.381
[secretary 2] Well, he's gathered us all, so apparently.

746
40:44.464 --> 40:46.299
[secretary 1] Do you think we should buy more shares?

747
40:46.383 --> 40:47.592
[secretary 3] Hmm, maybe so…

748
40:54.307 --> 40:56.393
[Na-jung] So you're Yoon Yi-jun's secretary.

749
41:01.398 --> 41:03.191
I'll admit, I was curious.

750
41:03.692 --> 41:05.443
I know he's very picky,

751
41:05.527 --> 41:08.405
so I wanted to see what's so special about you.

752
41:08.488 --> 41:13.076
[clicks tongue]

753
41:16.579 --> 41:18.456
I guess I'll have to wait and find out.

754
41:18.540 --> 41:20.458
Why don't you name your price?

755
41:21.209 --> 41:22.794
[tense music playing]

756
41:22.877 --> 41:24.796
What exactly do you need from me?

757
41:24.879 --> 41:26.923
I'd heard that you're pretty quick.

758
41:28.133 --> 41:30.552
What do you think I need from my brother's secretary?

759
41:30.635 --> 41:32.429
Information, obviously.

760
41:33.638 --> 41:35.807
[Jae-hee] I can tell it's not the first time she's done this.

761
41:37.225 --> 41:40.562
I bet she's said this exact same thing to Yoon Yi-jun's other aides.

762
41:41.938 --> 41:43.398
Thanks.

763
41:44.441 --> 41:45.775
I have to get going.

764
41:46.609 --> 41:49.112
I look forward to hearing your decision.

765
41:50.739 --> 41:51.781
I'll tell you right now.

766
41:53.408 --> 41:55.076
I won't be part of it.

767
41:55.160 --> 41:57.162
[tense music continues]

768
42:04.919 --> 42:10.216
How many others… have you approached and given that same speech?

769
42:11.426 --> 42:13.720
Did Ms. Han hear the same offer?

770
42:13.803 --> 42:15.305
[chuckles]

771
42:15.889 --> 42:17.474
You were supposed to be quick.

772
42:19.601 --> 42:20.477
Hey.

773
42:21.644 --> 42:25.357
For little nobodies like you, connections are critical.

774
42:27.108 --> 42:28.818
So you should accept the offer.

775
42:28.902 --> 42:30.570
Thank you.

776
42:31.154 --> 42:33.448
I think I can handle things just fine without it.

777
42:33.531 --> 42:35.241
[scoffs]

778
42:38.119 --> 42:40.413
Oh, Yi-jun. I hear you're on sick leave.

779
42:40.497 --> 42:42.874
I'm heading to Fiji soon, so you should come.

780
42:42.957 --> 42:45.168
It'll be good to get some fresh air. How about it?

781
42:46.753 --> 42:48.588
I don't think I'm sick enough to warrant that.

782
42:51.925 --> 42:55.095
I want to apologize and express my gratitude for the invitation.

783
42:57.180 --> 42:58.390
[door opens]

784
43:01.810 --> 43:03.019
Na-jung, you're here!

785
43:04.646 --> 43:06.398
And so are you, Mr. Na.

786
43:07.565 --> 43:08.858
[Mr. Na] Uh…

787
43:09.442 --> 43:12.612
You're right. I don't really have a right to be here.

788
43:13.530 --> 43:15.698
Oh, you have every right to join us, Uncle.

789
43:15.782 --> 43:18.701
Really, it's quite an occasion after all.

790
43:18.785 --> 43:19.911
[both chuckle]

791
43:19.994 --> 43:23.331
I've noticed Retail's year-over-year operating profit's increased a lot.

792
43:23.415 --> 43:24.374
[chuckles]

793
43:25.083 --> 43:27.377
It's done well since Ms. Yoon took over, hasn't it?

794
43:27.460 --> 43:30.422
[scoffs] Retail usually comes in second.

795
43:31.256 --> 43:33.341
Winning this time was just a stroke of luck.

796
43:34.092 --> 43:35.510
No need to flatter yourself.

797
43:38.680 --> 43:39.806
I'll work harder.

798
43:40.473 --> 43:42.976
Even given your famously high expectations,

799
43:43.059 --> 43:45.061
I believe Yi-jun's proven himself.

800
43:45.145 --> 43:46.896
He's worthy of your trust.

801
43:46.980 --> 43:47.814
[Mr. Na chuckles]

802
43:47.897 --> 43:50.191
He's led the TF team this far, which has been difficult.

803
43:50.275 --> 43:53.111
I think he'll go far. Let's all have faith in him.

804
43:54.112 --> 43:58.324
[laughs]

805
44:00.743 --> 44:02.704
-Show us. -Ah, yes, sir.

806
44:19.637 --> 44:22.140
[tense music playing]

807
44:24.017 --> 44:25.935
TAEKANG RETAIL STOCK PURCHASE AGREEMENT

808
44:53.838 --> 44:56.299
TAEKANG RETAIL STOCK PURCHASE AGREEMENT

809
45:01.221 --> 45:03.097
[tense music continues]

810
45:05.433 --> 45:06.768
I said to stay out of trouble.

811
45:07.644 --> 45:09.896
I asked so little, but you still let me down.

812
45:09.979 --> 45:10.939
You're not ready to lead us.

813
45:15.860 --> 45:20.615
I'll hand over the company to whichever subsidiary maintains Taekang's lead.

814
45:20.698 --> 45:21.741
Listen closely.

815
45:26.454 --> 45:28.081
I want to see results.

816
45:29.666 --> 45:31.459
My successor…

817
45:32.043 --> 45:34.212
shall be announced at the next meeting.

818
45:35.380 --> 45:38.466
[clanging]

819
45:41.386 --> 45:42.554
Let's eat.

820
45:43.137 --> 45:44.556
[chair scrapes]

821
45:51.187 --> 45:52.188
Congrats.

822
45:53.439 --> 45:55.024
You should take some time off.

823
45:55.108 --> 45:58.111
[uneasy music playing]

824
46:01.197 --> 46:02.574
[music ends]

825
46:03.825 --> 46:05.285
What the heck just happened?

826
46:06.911 --> 46:08.162
I know, right?

827
46:09.163 --> 46:10.999
You really dropped the ball.

828
46:11.082 --> 46:13.501
You can't even take what's handed to you.

829
46:14.294 --> 46:17.046
When you can't tell whether you're being served alcohol…

830
46:18.590 --> 46:20.008
or poison,

831
46:20.550 --> 46:22.844
you just gotta man up and take a drink.

832
46:22.927 --> 46:26.264
So what you just drank was poisonous?

833
46:27.890 --> 46:29.475
[chuckles]

834
46:29.559 --> 46:31.686
[tense music playing]

835
46:31.769 --> 46:34.981
What did I tell you? You should've taken the offer.

836
46:36.983 --> 46:39.360
It looks like your master's been cut off.

837
46:40.695 --> 46:42.572
You bet on the wrong horse.

838
47:02.550 --> 47:03.885
Need some consoling, sir?

839
47:06.846 --> 47:09.807
To be honest, consolation's not my strong suit,

840
47:09.891 --> 47:10.892
but I'll give it a try.

841
47:13.019 --> 47:16.814
In life, we're all given an equal share of fortunes and misfortunes,

842
47:17.398 --> 47:20.401
which means since you experienced one misfortune today,

843
47:20.485 --> 47:22.820
you can expect one fortune in the near future.

844
47:22.904 --> 47:24.906
Just drive the car.

845
47:26.157 --> 47:28.701
-Yep. -I predicted this.

846
47:30.620 --> 47:32.914
I didn't simply go 'cause I lost the bet with you.

847
47:32.997 --> 47:36.250
I chose to go 'cause I wanted to.

848
47:36.334 --> 47:39.253
Oh, so you knew the chairman would do that?

849
47:40.922 --> 47:42.215
You're being so loyal.

850
47:42.674 --> 47:44.092
I thought this was just a job to you.

851
47:45.635 --> 47:47.345
-[car horn honking] -[tires screeching]

852
47:47.428 --> 47:49.722
-[Jae-hee] Whoa. -[Yi-jun grunts]

853
47:50.598 --> 47:51.432
You okay, sir?

854
47:52.892 --> 47:54.477
[gentle music playing]

855
47:54.560 --> 47:55.728
I'm so sorry.

856
47:56.062 --> 47:57.939
That was just a reflex. I was worried you were hurt.

857
48:00.608 --> 48:01.943
"Worried I was hurt"?

858
48:02.026 --> 48:04.404
I'm being overprotective, as you said earlier.

859
48:05.947 --> 48:09.325
I have to consider your safety. After all, I'm your inner circle.

860
48:12.912 --> 48:15.581
You're presumptuous. You're no such thing.

861
48:18.251 --> 48:19.419
[sighs]

862
48:27.260 --> 48:29.804
LEGAL DEPARTMENT LAWYER KIM SI-HYUN

863
48:29.887 --> 48:32.181
[pensive music playing]

864
48:32.265 --> 48:34.684
[Si-hyun] You're only interested in me for my work.

865
48:35.309 --> 48:38.062
That's why you asked me out, right?

866
48:39.814 --> 48:41.691
The other thing didn't fall through.

867
48:42.150 --> 48:43.276
I wanted to see you.

868
48:44.402 --> 48:46.404
SAESUPGIL HAEJANGGUK

869
48:46.487 --> 48:48.531
[phone buzzing]

870
48:49.949 --> 48:51.909
SECRETARY LEE HYE-JUNG

871
48:58.875 --> 49:01.627
[automated voice] The caller you are trying to reach is unavailable.

872
49:01.711 --> 49:03.379
Please leave a message.

873
49:14.098 --> 49:16.267
I've confirmed your security system's working fine.

874
49:16.350 --> 49:17.560
I'll be heading out now.

875
49:18.269 --> 49:19.437
Want a drink?

876
49:20.062 --> 49:21.856
No thanks, sir. I'd better go.

877
49:22.440 --> 49:23.649
Okay, then.

878
49:28.362 --> 49:29.697
[cork pops]

879
49:35.870 --> 49:36.954
All right, fine.

880
49:37.038 --> 49:39.081
But I'm charging overtime, and won't be drinking.

881
49:39.165 --> 49:41.167
I'll be here for you if you need someone.

882
49:42.293 --> 49:43.169
You're a lightweight?

883
49:43.961 --> 49:45.588
[Captain Park] You are strictly forbidden to drink!

884
49:45.671 --> 49:47.632
You'll blow this operation the moment you get drunk

885
49:47.715 --> 49:50.468
and start acting up as always. Mark my words.

886
49:50.802 --> 49:52.929
[sighs] I can't, I'm sorry.

887
49:53.012 --> 49:56.098
If that's not the case, then one drink won't hurt.

888
49:59.185 --> 50:01.562
-Okay, sir. In exchange-- -"In exchange…"

889
50:03.606 --> 50:05.900
Why does there have to be a catch for everything?

890
50:06.526 --> 50:08.361
Can't you just do as I say without questioning?

891
50:09.737 --> 50:11.113
If we're going to drink,

892
50:11.197 --> 50:13.574
why don't we make it fun and play a little game together.

893
50:14.242 --> 50:15.493
On one condition.

894
50:15.952 --> 50:17.745
You answer one question truthfully.

895
50:17.829 --> 50:21.874
[tense music playing]

896
50:34.470 --> 50:38.057
Mr. Kim, did you know that dogs…

897
50:39.100 --> 50:40.977
don't get to choose their masters?

898
50:42.103 --> 50:44.230
The masters do all the choosing.

899
50:46.148 --> 50:48.025
Why don't you come out with it?

900
50:48.109 --> 50:49.527
Who are you serving?

901
50:57.159 --> 50:58.244
First of all,

902
50:59.245 --> 51:00.538
I'm not a dog.

903
51:01.330 --> 51:03.040
But to answer your question,

904
51:04.041 --> 51:05.710
Taekang's my master.

905
51:05.793 --> 51:07.837
And if I take over Taekang?

906
51:10.798 --> 51:12.008
Oh.

907
51:12.091 --> 51:13.968
I guess that one's difficult.

908
51:14.760 --> 51:16.012
I'll make this easier.

909
51:17.305 --> 51:19.515
Where is Mr. Park Min-hwan right now?

910
51:24.312 --> 51:25.396
[Yi-jun gasps]

911
51:26.022 --> 51:30.359
Of all the things I heard this year, that was the rudest!

912
51:30.443 --> 51:34.488
[thick-tongued] Ugh, please, give me a break. I'm just saying what I think.

913
51:34.572 --> 51:35.656
What's the big deal?

914
51:35.740 --> 51:39.952
But still, hey, it's what you're into, so I'm not judging.

915
51:40.036 --> 51:42.330
[laughs] Oh, oh…

916
51:43.289 --> 51:44.498
[sighs]

917
51:44.916 --> 51:46.125
[giggles]

918
51:48.419 --> 51:50.963
Okay. I wanna hear it again.

919
51:52.173 --> 51:53.507
Once more.

920
51:53.591 --> 51:55.301
[chuckles] I can repeat myself now?

921
51:55.384 --> 51:57.053
Please just say it.

922
51:57.136 --> 51:59.597
[playful music playing]

923
52:00.890 --> 52:02.808
You're dorky for collecting them.

924
52:03.184 --> 52:04.518
-"Dorky"? -Dorky.

925
52:05.436 --> 52:09.523
I mean, of all the crazy things you could be into.

926
52:09.607 --> 52:11.275
[shivering]

927
52:12.777 --> 52:14.737
Pervert. You otaku.

928
52:14.820 --> 52:17.865
Pervert? Otaku?

929
52:17.949 --> 52:19.575
[laughs]

930
52:19.659 --> 52:20.493
You're crazy.

931
52:20.576 --> 52:22.703
[laughs] That's hilarious.

932
52:23.245 --> 52:24.872
-Come here. -I will not!

933
52:25.414 --> 52:26.582
[screams] Hey!

934
52:27.333 --> 52:28.334
Joking!

935
52:31.420 --> 52:35.216
"Come here," like I haven't already seen it. [chuckles]

936
52:39.303 --> 52:42.765
Well, since you've so graciously opened the door!

937
52:43.349 --> 52:44.225
Why not?

938
52:46.602 --> 52:48.646
-[gasps] -[lively, upbeat music playing]

939
52:48.729 --> 52:51.440
Wow! This is…

940
52:52.108 --> 52:53.609
You put lights in and everything!

941
52:54.360 --> 52:56.195
[chuckles] Whoa…

942
52:57.530 --> 52:59.615
Wow, seriously, get a load of this!

943
53:00.282 --> 53:03.119
[lively, upbeat music continues]

944
53:12.837 --> 53:16.048
These girls' bodies are like, whoa! Is this how they get the bad guys?

945
53:16.132 --> 53:17.216
ARA, THE SEA GODDESS

946
53:17.299 --> 53:19.218
By wowing them with their crazy curves?

947
53:20.094 --> 53:24.807
Welp, okay… if that's what you're looking for specifically,

948
53:24.890 --> 53:27.476
I guess I was right, you're a perv.

949
53:27.810 --> 53:29.687
Perverted otaku. [chuckles]

950
53:29.770 --> 53:31.313
-Shut your mouth. -[Jae-hee chuckles]

951
53:31.397 --> 53:32.773
[gasps]

952
53:32.857 --> 53:33.899
That's so scary.

953
53:34.608 --> 53:37.486
Hey, this is the one that freaked me out the last time I was here.

954
53:38.404 --> 53:40.614
Why did they have to go and make her so hugeful?

955
53:41.657 --> 53:44.368
You know what? She's growing on me.

956
53:45.494 --> 53:46.454
Ara.

957
53:49.999 --> 53:51.042
Oh… [chuckles]

958
53:51.917 --> 53:54.587
-Is this her special shrine? -Oh, don't touch.

959
53:55.046 --> 53:56.047
Off-limits.

960
53:58.841 --> 54:01.469
Okay, fine, I won't touch it. [whines]

961
54:01.552 --> 54:03.012
-Okay… -Okay!

962
54:03.095 --> 54:04.638
[grunts] Time for another round.

963
54:07.433 --> 54:10.352
I'm turned on by strong women who can hold their own.

964
54:10.728 --> 54:12.938
[Yi-jun] And you think that makes me a pervert?

965
54:13.731 --> 54:14.899
[sighs]

966
54:15.191 --> 54:16.400
Otaku?

967
54:18.277 --> 54:20.279
[scoffs] Seriously.

968
54:21.280 --> 54:23.199
Do I really deserve to be mocked?

969
54:23.282 --> 54:24.575
[Jae-hee] Mm.

970
54:25.910 --> 54:27.328
Come on, I didn't…

971
54:27.828 --> 54:29.955
I don't think I said anything that harsh.

972
54:30.039 --> 54:31.373
[giggles]

973
54:31.457 --> 54:32.416
No?

974
54:33.417 --> 54:37.880
Not only was I mocked, but you made fun of my ideal type of a woman as a whole.

975
54:37.963 --> 54:39.423
-Oh. -Say sorry.

976
54:39.507 --> 54:41.217
Okay.

977
54:43.010 --> 54:45.513
Sorry, I sincerely apologize.

978
54:47.264 --> 54:48.140
Was that enough?

979
54:49.934 --> 54:51.060
You know what?

980
54:51.143 --> 54:54.480
Now that I'm back in here, seeing all the nice colors…

981
54:55.314 --> 54:56.982
it feels like a superhero museum.

982
54:57.066 --> 54:58.109
I like it.

983
54:59.693 --> 55:02.071
The doll you said not to touch, that one.

984
55:03.572 --> 55:04.824
That's your prized possession?

985
55:06.158 --> 55:07.243
I guess it is.

986
55:08.452 --> 55:12.039
That's the final gift my mother gave me before she died.

987
55:12.123 --> 55:13.707
[gentle sentimental music playing]

988
55:13.791 --> 55:18.796
[Yi-jun's mom] Yi-jun, Ara here will always keep you safe.

989
55:18.879 --> 55:20.756
-Okay? -Uh-huh.

990
55:20.923 --> 55:21.924
[Yi-jun's mom] Here, sweetie.

991
55:23.008 --> 55:24.385
[young Yi-jun] Wow.

992
55:24.844 --> 55:26.428
[chuckles]

993
55:26.512 --> 55:29.140
I made it myself, just for you. Do you like it?

994
55:29.223 --> 55:30.474
Mm-hmm. Yeah.

995
55:31.892 --> 55:33.811
[gentle piano music playing]

996
55:33.894 --> 55:36.105
[giggles]

997
55:37.523 --> 55:38.524
[Jae-hee] Hey, wait…

998
55:39.275 --> 55:42.236
All these ladies in here, they're all heroes, huh?

999
55:43.612 --> 55:44.446
[laughs]

1000
55:46.824 --> 55:49.076
You wanted to be a hero as a kid?

1001
55:49.160 --> 55:51.787
-[gasps] Aww, such a cutie. -[clicks tongue]

1002
55:52.413 --> 55:53.914
I wanted to protect everyone,

1003
55:55.457 --> 55:58.127
and in the end I couldn't protect anyone.

1004
55:59.503 --> 56:01.839
Instead, I collected all these trinkets.

1005
56:02.298 --> 56:03.424
[Jae-hee] Guess so…

1006
56:04.049 --> 56:08.220
I mean, if I'm being honest, you're not cool enough to be a hero.

1007
56:08.721 --> 56:10.973
I'd say that's probably your biggest flaw.

1008
56:11.098 --> 56:12.641
You've got a crappy personality.

1009
56:13.142 --> 56:16.020
Being around you makes me wanna get drunk. [groans]

1010
56:16.687 --> 56:18.355
So alcohol makes you really obnoxious?

1011
56:19.190 --> 56:23.319
I will say… you and these girls have one thing in common.

1012
56:25.321 --> 56:28.741
When you decide that someone needs protection, you do it.

1013
56:29.241 --> 56:31.202
That's not an easy thing, you know.

1014
56:32.411 --> 56:34.163
It takes a ton of courage.

1015
56:34.246 --> 56:35.581
Courage.

1016
56:36.832 --> 56:38.292
Not really,

1017
56:38.959 --> 56:40.920
I don't think I've protected anyone.

1018
56:42.087 --> 56:43.088
Hmm?

1019
56:48.260 --> 56:50.554
You did. You looked out for me.

1020
56:54.767 --> 56:58.354
You were worried I'd be in danger if I knew what was going on,

1021
56:58.437 --> 57:00.981
so you were so nasty.

1022
57:01.065 --> 57:03.150
You really bullied me so hard.

1023
57:04.985 --> 57:05.819
Didn't you?

1024
57:08.864 --> 57:11.242
And I bet Ms. Han was treated the same way.

1025
57:12.159 --> 57:16.497
What you said at the columbarium, I know the person you blame is you.

1026
57:17.539 --> 57:18.624
I can tell.

1027
57:18.707 --> 57:20.709
[gentle music playing]

1028
57:24.255 --> 57:26.840
Where did you get the nerve to say all that?

1029
57:28.926 --> 57:30.928
I just think you let people assume

1030
57:31.512 --> 57:33.847
you're a worse boss than you really are.

1031
57:34.431 --> 57:37.184
We just met, and even I can see who you truly are.

1032
57:37.268 --> 57:39.645
I think your mom and Ms. Han could, too.

1033
57:42.231 --> 57:44.858
They saw who you really are. Mm.

1034
57:48.445 --> 57:49.571
[sniffles]

1035
57:50.698 --> 57:52.992
I thought I said to stop crossing boundaries.

1036
57:54.618 --> 57:56.578
Why are you… [breathing shakily]

1037
57:57.746 --> 58:00.207
noticing the things I don't want anyone to know?

1038
58:06.547 --> 58:07.798
[exhales]

1039
58:08.424 --> 58:09.717
I'll leave you alone.

1040
58:12.261 --> 58:13.595
When the game's done.

1041
58:16.390 --> 58:19.768
Answer one question, like you promised you would.

1042
58:24.982 --> 58:26.650
You didn't really kill her…

1043
58:28.861 --> 58:29.695
did you?

1044
58:37.494 --> 58:38.412
Ms. Han…

1045
58:40.581 --> 58:42.291
didn't die because of you.

1046
58:53.594 --> 58:54.762
She didn't.

1047
58:57.389 --> 58:58.682
[sighs]

1048
59:00.309 --> 59:01.518
That's good enough for me.

1049
59:02.102 --> 59:03.979
[gentle music playing]

1050
59:07.941 --> 59:08.942
Special Forces?

1051
59:11.278 --> 59:12.112
Are you okay?

1052
59:13.655 --> 59:14.740
[gasps]

1053
59:15.407 --> 59:16.784
Did you seriously just fall asleep?

1054
59:20.829 --> 59:21.830
Wake up.

1055
59:23.624 --> 59:25.793
Mr. Kang, just sit up for a second.

1056
59:26.293 --> 59:27.378
[groans]

1057
59:28.170 --> 59:29.797
-[Jerry meows] -Mm?

1058
59:31.256 --> 59:32.299
Oh, my gosh!

1059
59:33.258 --> 59:34.718
[playful orchestral music playing]

1060
59:34.802 --> 59:36.762
-You… -Whoa!

1061
59:38.138 --> 59:39.306
[Jae-hee] Get back here!

1062
59:40.849 --> 59:42.518
You sneaky little stinker!

1063
59:42.601 --> 59:44.478
[Jerry meows]

1064
59:44.561 --> 59:46.021
[mimics meow loudly]

1065
59:48.190 --> 59:49.817
Come back, Yi-jun junior!

1066
59:53.195 --> 59:54.321
[chuckles]

1067
59:55.114 --> 59:58.117
[playful orchestral music continues]

1068
01:00:01.829 --> 01:00:03.122
Huh?

1069
01:00:08.919 --> 01:00:09.962
[yells] Stay there!

1070
01:00:10.045 --> 01:00:11.213
[Jerry meows]

1071
01:00:15.467 --> 01:00:17.428
Little brat! Get back here!

1072
01:00:17.511 --> 01:00:20.139
You little monster!

1073
01:00:20.222 --> 01:00:22.933
-[screams] -[Jerry meows]

1074
01:00:24.685 --> 01:00:26.353
Ugh, that cat's a jerk.

1075
01:00:26.437 --> 01:00:28.021
[panting]

1076
01:00:28.105 --> 01:00:30.357
How dare you make me work out, hm?

1077
01:00:31.150 --> 01:00:32.317
Where you at?!

1078
01:00:32.901 --> 01:00:36.071
[panting]

1079
01:00:41.326 --> 01:00:44.329
You. I've got you now.

1080
01:00:44.830 --> 01:00:50.294
But you should know that Special Forces can catch anything.

1081
01:00:51.545 --> 01:00:53.213
Ha! So you wanna go?

1082
01:00:54.006 --> 01:00:55.424
-Don't gimme that look! -[hisses]

1083
01:00:56.592 --> 01:00:57.676
Here I come.

1084
01:00:58.218 --> 01:01:01.180
One, two…

1085
01:01:03.140 --> 01:01:04.933
[Jerry growls]

1086
01:01:05.017 --> 01:01:06.643
Three!

1087
01:01:07.352 --> 01:01:08.395
[grunts]

1088
01:01:08.479 --> 01:01:11.648
-[Yi-jun] That's enough. -Wait, what? What the heck?

1089
01:01:12.691 --> 01:01:16.111
Ugh, seriously. What are you doing?!

1090
01:01:16.195 --> 01:01:18.238
[grunts] Who the hell…

1091
01:01:19.531 --> 01:01:20.699
[groans in pain]

1092
01:01:22.993 --> 01:01:24.953
[coughing]

1093
01:01:27.414 --> 01:01:28.457
Why are you like this?

1094
01:01:29.249 --> 01:01:30.459
Get some self-control.

1095
01:01:30.542 --> 01:01:32.920
You're really overdoing it.

1096
01:01:33.003 --> 01:01:34.505
[blows air]

1097
01:01:35.172 --> 01:01:37.382
Who the hell hits someone,

1098
01:01:39.259 --> 01:01:41.512
then runs off before the fight?!

1099
01:01:43.055 --> 01:01:44.097
[Jae-hee grunts]

1100
01:01:44.181 --> 01:01:49.186
-Whoa, whoa! Special Forces, no! -[upbeat quirky music playing]

1101
01:01:49.269 --> 01:01:50.312
[Jae-hee] Gotcha!

1102
01:01:50.395 --> 01:01:52.481
-Anything you say can be used against you. -[yelps in pain]

1103
01:01:53.273 --> 01:01:54.107
Get ready…

1104
01:01:54.858 --> 01:01:55.734
-[Jae-hee] Whoa, what? -Ugh, get off.

1105
01:01:55.817 --> 01:01:57.945
-Where're my handcuffs? -Get off my back!

1106
01:01:58.028 --> 01:01:59.446
[groans]

1107
01:01:59.530 --> 01:02:01.573
-[grunts] -[Yi-jun] Get off!

1108
01:02:03.575 --> 01:02:06.245
-[groaning] -God, Special Forces!

1109
01:02:14.461 --> 01:02:16.964
-Get back here! -[screams]

1110
01:02:19.508 --> 01:02:22.469
[romantic music playing]

1111
01:03:25.991 --> 01:03:29.911
LOVE IN DISGUISE

1112
01:03:29.995 --> 01:03:31.997
[closing theme music playing]

1113
01:03:52.643 --> 01:03:53.935
SPECIAL THANKS TO KIM DO-YOON AND JUNG YOO-MIN FOR THEIR APPEARANCE

1114
01:03:54.019 --> 01:03:57.105
[Jae-hee] The real culprit's out there. They're definitely after Yoon Yi-jun.

1115
01:03:57.189 --> 01:03:58.440
[Seok-jin] Yoon Yi-jun's fiancé is coming back.

1116
01:03:58.523 --> 01:03:59.733
[Wan-gu] The daughter of a presidential frontrunner,

1117
01:03:59.816 --> 01:04:00.817
she's protected.

1118
01:04:00.901 --> 01:04:01.860
You slept together?

1119
01:04:01.943 --> 01:04:03.111
-Not at all! -Are you crazy?

1120
01:04:03.195 --> 01:04:05.864
[Yi-jun] I did it because I was disgusted with my secretary.

1121
01:04:05.947 --> 01:04:08.617
-A little more? Tiny bit? -Cute…

1122
01:04:08.700 --> 01:04:09.868
[Seok-jin] We have to find them.

1123
01:04:09.951 --> 01:04:13.622
[Na-jung] If you bring me Park Min-hwan, I'll tell you what you're dying to know.

1124
01:04:13.705 --> 01:04:16.249
[Yi-jun] I'll do what I can to prevent any further damage.

1125
01:04:16.833 --> 01:04:17.709
You got somewhere to hide?

1126
01:04:17.793 --> 01:04:18.919
Yoon Na-jung?

1127
01:04:19.294 --> 01:04:20.879
[Yi-jun] I gotta go, I need to check up on something.
